- How would you rotate device keys without interrupting service?
- How would you detect and mitigate poisoned shares in real time?

## Why This Is Asked
The tokenized explanation approach isolates training data exposure, supporting privacy and auditability for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- JWT-based explanation tokens, HS256 signing
- model_versioning, token rotation, expiry
- input validation and per-user audit

## Code Example
```javascript
// Issue explain token (Node.js)
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function issueExplainToken(user_id, model_version, expiryMs, secret) {
  const payload = { sub: user_id, mv: model_version, exp: Math.floor(Date.now()/1000) + expiryMs/1000 };
  return jwt.sign(payload, secret, { algorithm: 'HS256', audience: user_id });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate signing keys and invalidate tokens after a model version update?
- How would you test for token forgery or replay attacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Schema evolution is common in production systems. This tests ability to plan backward-compatible changes that don’t break existing clients.

## Key Concepts
- API versioning and data contracts
- Migration scripts and defaulting
- Feature flags and canary rollouts
- Regression and contract tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Migration mapping
function migrate(payload) {
  if (payload.score_source) return payload;
  if (payload.model_version >= 2) payload.score_source = 'model';
  else payload.score_source = 'heuristic';
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rollback a failed migration?
- Which tests best validate both old and new clients?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design a privacy-preserving ABAC layer that controls access to encrypted CCA score shares without revealing plaintext data. It tests understanding of dynamic admin access, revocation mechanisms, auditability, and system design at scale.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC attributes: tenant_id, region, role, expiry
- Token-based access without decryption
- Immutable audit logs with tamper-evident provenance
- Key management with per-tenant keys
- Revocation and expiry propagation

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePolicy(attrs, action) {
  const now = Date.now();

  if (attrs.expiry < now) return { allowed: false, reason: 'expired' };
  if (!attrs.tenant_id || !attrs.region) return { allowed: false, reason: 'missing attributes' };

  const policy = getPolicy(attrs.policy_id);
  if (!policy) return { allowed: false, reason: 'policy not found' };

  const regionMatch = policy.regions.includes(attrs.region);
  const roleMatch = policy.roles.includes(attrs.role);

  return { allowed: regionMatch && roleMatch, reason: regionMatch && roleMatch ? 'ok' : 'attribute mismatch' };
}

function revokeAccess(policyId, reason) {
  const policy = getPolicy(policyId);
  policy.revoked = true;
  policy.revocationReason = reason;
  publishRevocationEvent(policyId);
}
```

